From: Ho Jie Feng <hjf3108@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mailbox: bcm-pdc: allow building on ARCH_BCMBCA

The SPU crypto engine of the Broadcom BCA (broadband) SoCs BCM4908,
BCM63158, BCM6858, BCM47622 and BCM6756 sits behind the same PDC
(FlexSparx dma64) ring manager as the one on Northstar 2, with the same
register layout and descriptor format. The Broadcom SDK drives it with a
fork of this driver (bcmdrivers/opensource/char/pdc/impl1/pdc.c).

Allow BCM_PDC_MBOX to be selected on ARCH_BCMBCA.

Signed-off-by: Ho Jie Feng <hjf3108@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/mailbox/Kconfig | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/mailbox/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/mailbox/Kconfig
@@ -250,11 +250,12 @@ config XGENE_SLIMPRO_MBOX
 
 config BCM_PDC_MBOX
 	tristate "Broadcom FlexSparx DMA Mailbox"
-	depends on ARCH_BCM_IPROC || COMPILE_TEST
+	depends on ARCH_BCM_IPROC || ARCH_BCMBCA || COMPILE_TEST
 	help
 	  Mailbox implementation for the Broadcom FlexSparx DMA ring manager,
 	  which provides access to various offload engines on Broadcom
-	  SoCs, including FA2/FA+ on Northstar Plus and PDC on Northstar 2.
+	  SoCs, including FA2/FA+ on Northstar Plus, PDC on Northstar 2 and
+	  the SPU PDC on BCA SoCs such as BCM4908 and BCM47622.
 
 config BCM_FLEXRM_MBOX
 	tristate "Broadcom FlexRM Mailbox"
